t built, not deleted â€” queued for build after Phase 6 (next 10 Hillsdale Online courses). Rationale: Phase 3 (completed 2026-05-04) supplied 22 candidate lectures (*American Heritage* Ã—12, *The Great American Story* Ã—10); building before Phase 6 adds the rest would force a rebuild. **Defer-then-build is cheaper than build-now-then-redo.**\n\n- **Elementary stubs (Phase 4 #4): four kept as real gaps, then partially built as stub-with-spec (Group B).**\n  - `elementary/grade-4/Grammar-Diagramming/` â€” confirmed a **real gap**, then **built as stub-with-spec (~1,300 words)**. Spine: Mary Daly *Diagramming the Sentences of the Catechism* (Reed-Kellogg primary) + Reed & Kellogg *Graded Lessons in English* 1875 (public-domain alternate). 6 units / 120 lessons / 60 hours, co-running with `K4-WRITING-WISE-BAUER-WWE`; synthesis instrument is **visual-diff machine grading on diagram correctness**.\n  - `elementary/grade-4/Writing-Wise-Bauer-WWE/` â€” real gap (WWE is the elementary precursor to the populated G5 WWS-1); build later.\n  - `elementary/grade-5/Grammar-Complete/` â€” real gap (capstone consolidating G3+G4 grammar); build later.\n\n### Cross-cutting observations\n\n- **Two-state disposition vocabulary in play:** *Reframed* / *Stub-with-spec built* (acted on now) vs *Keep as real gap* / *Defer* (queued). The log distinguishes a true content gap from a legacy-naming artifact.\n- **Sandbox constraint surfaced repeatedly:** directory renames are deferred to a **supervised cleanup pass** because the sandbox cannot rename â€” a recurring downstream action item, not a decision.\n- **Sequencing discipline:** multiple decisions (Am-History, elementary builds) are gated on later phases (6, future Wave-2-elementary) to avoid rework â€” the log consistently prefers defer-then-build over build-then-redo.\n\nOne note on fidelity: the anchors are truncated mid-table in several places (Group A's `middle/grade-8/Moderâ€¦` row, Group B's WWE row, the Phase 4 #4 G5 row), so the 